<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bastia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bastia is a port city in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corsica">Corsica</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, founded by the Genoese around 1380 around a fortress (bastiglia) that gave it its name. It was the capital of Corsica under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> and the seat of the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> during the Anglo-Corsican Kingdom of 1794–1796. It remains the island's main commercial port.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bastia.jpg" alt="Bastia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cosudibastia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bastia,_A_Marina,_Vechju_Portu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
